      "sourceTextSha256": "e9ad39d0c0959fac80abec28c2683611a0e523e0ca9319451391db078260d961",
      "text": "San José to the Pacific coast",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mwa8yawe-gv8kp71s5",
        "model": "GPT-6 Codex"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "7fef550e241213a670f16e69d9c2b72437674558ad7a3cbcd05865d9a739323e",
      "text": "Have breakfast at the hotel, then transfer to the Pacific coast. The drive takes about 4 hours.\n\nThe main fishing area is around Flamingo on Costa Rica’s northwestern coast. About 20 miles west of the port, the water deepens from 360 feet to 2,000 feet or more. These waters are home to sailfish, blue, black and striped marlin, dorado, yellowfin tuna and bigeye tuna.\n\nThe Catalina and Brummel islands are about 5 miles from Flamingo harbour. Wahoo, sierra mackerel, Spanish mackerel, bigeye jack, several species of perch and roosterfish are caught here year-round.\n\nOvernight at **Tamarindo Diria**.\n\nMeals: breakfast and lunch.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mwa8yawe-gv8kp71s5",
        "model": "GPT-6 Codex"
      }
